        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 5:02PM CDT by NWS Norman OK</headline>
        <description>At 502 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm just
northwest of Lawton, or over southern Fort Sill, moving northeast at
25 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Elgin, Medicine Park, Fort Sill, Lake Ellsworth, Lake Lawtonka,
eastern Wichita Mountains Wildlife Refuge, and Mount Scott.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
